=== D. Generating function and Dirichlet series
PASS generating function: the geometric-series formula reproduces m(d) for 1 <= d <= 200000 (first exponent (2^v-4)/6 for even v, (5*2^v-16)/6 for odd v)
PASS 2^v - 3 = 1 (mod 6) for even v and = 5 (mod 6) for odd v, so 6d+1 = q_v * s with s = 1 or 5 (mod 6)
    s=2: partial sum (d<=1e8) 1.045530405547044, tail <= 8.56e-09, closed form 1.04553040592028546
PASS Dirichlet series identity F(s) = (L(s,chi0)Q(s) + L(s,chi)Q^-(s))/2 holds numerically at s = 2
    s=3: partial sum (d<=1e8) 1.004220493937064, tail <= 6.97e-18, closed form 1.00422049393706371
PASS Dirichlet series identity F(s) = (L(s,chi0)Q(s) + L(s,chi)Q^-(s))/2 holds numerically at s = 3
PASS continuation formula Q(s) = 1 + sum_j (s)_j/j! 3^j 2^(-3(s+j))/(1-2^(-(s+j))) matches the series at s = 1, 2 (and Q^- at s = 2)
PASS Q^-(0) = 1/2; Q has residue 1/ln2 at s = 0 and (-3)^1/ln2 at s = -1 (numerically)
PASS F(0) = 1/6 (F(+-1e-15) through the continuation; L(0,chi_-3) = 1/3), and (s-1)F(s) -> Q(1)/6 at s = 1
    Q(1) = 1.3436734331817690185 ; Q^-(1) = 0.8534750315118473507 ; residue of F at s=1 is Q(1)/6 = 0.22394557219696150309
