PASS S(X) = X^2/2 + O(X): |S(X) - X^2/2| <= 2X on the sample (the proof gives O(X))
PASS K is 2-regular: a(n) = K_(n+1), b(n) = K_(2n+2) satisfy a(2n) = n, a(2n+1) = b(n), b(2n) = a(n) + 6n + 2, b(2n+1) = 5n + 4  (n < 10^5)
